different ways of organizing data on your computer that can be used effectively    

constant time O(1): example : if you want to access any element from array using index 
--whatever the index maybe it will need the same time constant time

linear time -- loop through array ele O(N)

logarithmic time-- binary search O(log n)

looking at every array index twice O(N^2)

exponential time complexity -- double recursion 

 main problem divided into sub problem use recursion

 recursion time complexity worst because use stack 
 in factorial prefer loop 



# to remove spaces from the input and output
rstrip() ---> remove space from right side
lstrip() ----> remove space from right side
strip() ----> remove spaces from both sides
 example :
scity=city.strip()